%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 04a7120080da2e64b9a8c9c5ffc33ba1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Fool
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SO_DialogNPC
  _name: Fool
  _portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a6b7122dc2e67e54fa68108f416c30df, type: 3}
  _cards:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: fc214faf4ac6b0a4b97e870477a16e3b, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 42dd8cb590775ae4b9fdfbdb2d9f3f7c, type: 2}
  _dialogPaths:
  - entries:
    - playerText: 
      npcText: "I am the Fool, employed by our gracious king to amuse and distract
        the court.  $I am the jester, the clown\u2014made for laughter and obedience."
    - playerText: What are you scheming?
      npcText: Nothing much. /Looks like this conversation is over/
    - playerText: 'You look like you have plans '
      npcText: 'What are you ? A spy ? '
    - playerText: "You seem angry\u2026 plotting something?"
      npcText: I stir whispers in the streets, but that is all you need to know.
    - playerText: "The people suffer\u2026 are you plotting to help them?"
      npcText: Soon the streets will rise, but timing is everything. One wrong move,
        and it will fail.
    - playerText: "Tell me everything\u2014I want to help the people and see justice
        done."
      npcText: I will light the spark of revolution. The people will rise against
        the court, but only if we strike at the right moment.
  - entries:
    - playerText: 
      npcText: Hello again my friend. Things seem to be moving along quite nicely.
    - playerText: What are you plotting now?
      npcText: Hah! Still nothing for you to meddle with. Step back.
    - playerText: Can you give me a hint of your plan?
      npcText: "\u2026A hint? No. Some things must stay hidden, for the people are
        not yet ready."
    - playerText: "The kingdom suffers\u2026 are you ready to act?"
      npcText: Soon. Patience is part of the game. Act too early and it all crumbles.
    - playerText: "I want to understand your vision\u2014I can help, if you trust
        me"
      npcText: "\u2026You may see the shape of it, but the streets themselves must
        decide the moment. Timing is everything."
    - playerText: Tell me everything. How will the people rise?
      npcText: "I will ignite the flames of rebellion. The kingdom\u2019s rot cannot
        last, and the people will follow if we strike at the perfect moment."
  - entries:
    - playerText: 
      npcText: "How many merry people are here today.  $Laughing, dancing\u2026 and
        I shall be working until dawn."
    - playerText: 
      npcText: Everything is ready.  $Soon it will all begin. $The revolution shall
        be glorious, and at last we will be free.
  - entries:
    - playerText: 
      npcText: The court will soon be dancing, and I shall be there to entertain
        them.  $Such is my cross to bear.
  - entries:
    - playerText: 
      npcText: "I am the Fool, employed by our gracious king to amuse and distract
        the court.  $I am the jester, the clown\u2014made for laughter and obedience."
